      "writtenOn": "2025-09-08T08:29:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ack re. filtering out the current provider from the other endpoint quota usage. I also agree that we should probably not cache the usage of other providers on the same endpoint. As you said, that could be very dynamic.\n\nRe. your last point I think we might want to look at some more concrete examples as that\u0027s easier to reason about. For the sake of simplicity let\u0027s just look at # of instances quota and plug those into the different formulas.\n\n1. Current: `min(cloud_quota, provider_resource_limits) - unmanaged_usage - this_provider_usage`\n2. My proposal: `min(cloud_quota - unmanaged_usage - other_provider_usage, provider_resource_limits) - this_provider_usage`\n3. Alternative: `min(cloud_quota, provider_resource_limits) - unmanaged_usage - other_provider_usage - this_provider_usage`\n\nI slightly changed your alternative to also consider the unmanaged usage as I think you meant to include that in `other_endpoint_usage`.\n\n#### Example A\n\nCloud quota: 100\nUnmanaged usage: 5\nOther Provider usage: 70\nProvider A limits: 50\nProvider A usage: 10\n(Cloud quota unused: 15)\n\n1. Current: `min(100, 50) - 5 - 10 \u003d 35`\n2. Proposed: `min(100 - 5 - 70, 50) - 10 \u003d 15`\n3. Alternative: `min(100, 50) - 5 - 70 - 10 \u003d -35`\n\n\n#### Example B\n\nCloud quota: inf\nUnmanaged usage: 5\nOther Provider usage: 70\nProvider A limits: 50\nProvider A usage: 10\n(Cloud quota unused: inf)\n\n1. Current: `min(inf, 50) - 5 - 10 \u003d 35`\n2. Proposed: `min(inf - 5 - 70, 50) - 10 \u003d 40`\n3. Alternative: `min(inf, 50) - 5 - 70 - 10 \u003d -35`\n\n\n#### Example C\n\nCloud quota: 100\nUnmanaged usage: 80\nOther Provider usage: 10\nProvider A limits: 50\nProvider A usage: 5\n(Cloud quota unused: 5)\n\n1. Current: `min(100, 50) - 80 - 10 \u003d -40`\n2. Proposed: `min(100 - 80 - 10, 50) - 5 \u003d 5`\n3. Alternative: `min(100, 50) - 80 - 10 - 5 \u003d -45`\n\n\n#### Example D\n\nCloud quota: 100\nUnmanaged usage: 10\nOther Provider usage: 70\nProvider A limits: 50\nProvider A usage: 10\n(Cloud quota unused: 10)\n\n1. Current: `min(100, 50) - 10 - 10 \u003d 30`\n2. Proposed: `min(100 - 10 - 70, 50) - 10 \u003d 10`\n3. Alternative: `min(100, 50) - 10 - 70 - 5 \u003d -35`\n\n#### Example E\n\nCloud quota: 100\nUnmanaged usage: 10\nOther Provider usage: 30\nProvider A limits: 50\nProvider A usage: 5\n(Cloud quota unused: 55)\n\n1. Current: `min(100, 50) - 10 - 5 \u003d 35`\n2. Proposed: `min(100 - 10 - 30, 50) - 5 \u003d 45`\n3. Alternative: `min(100, 50) - 10 - 30 - 5 \u003d 5`\n\n---\n\nFrom those examples I still think that my proposal calculates the available quota for a provider correctly.",
